  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "生態學",
    "sub_ename": "ECOLOGY",
    "describe_ch": "本課程之主要目的在於介紹生態學之基本觀念，並說明與本系學術領域相關之河川生態系與坡地生態系主要特徵，最後要求同學透過如生態社區、生態城市、生態旅遊、生態材料、生態農村等國內近年漸受關注之生態單元，進行分組研討及分享。本課程希望藉由增進對生態學之瞭解，有助於同學日後參與水利工程或水土保育之規畫設計時，能夠充分考量生態系保育之必要性。",
    "describe_eh": "The main purpose of this course is to introduce the basic concepts of ecology and explain the main characteristics of river ecosystems and hillslope ecosystems related to the academic domains of our department. Students will be designated to new developing topics, such as eco-community, eco-city, eco-tourism, eco-material, and eco-village, for group discussions and presentation. This course aims to enhance the understandings of ecology and help students to fully consider the necessity of ecological conservation when participating in the planning and design of water resources engineering and conservation in the future.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
